[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/talk/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n4_thomas"
text = "# DRAFT
# Thomas at dusk, at his mortar in the infirmary (night 4, fog; the house fasts, no supper).
# If he hid the porter from the hunter last night (n3_thomas_hid_you), he gives him a story for it: he was here, for his head.
# Brother Simon out at night: he says it first (n4_thomas_simon) unless the porter has already heard it from him tonight
# (the dusk scene should set the same flag), then comes back to it. True, and it costs him nothing: he sends Simon out.
# Telling him about the crypt is reporting it the safe way (trust +5). Edwin poured out his sleeping draught; Thomas watched.
# Claims: n4_thomas_keeps (lie): Simon is a quiet man who keeps things. The men he points at are innocent, and he sent Simon out himself.
== start
(Fog presses at the infirmary window. Thomas is at his mortar, humming, as if it weren't there.)
Thomas {warm}: Alric. Come in, and shut the door on that. It gets into the chest.
-> hid [if n3_thomas_hid_you]
-> simon_back [if n4_thomas_simon]
-> simon_first

== hid
Thomas {warm}: You're whole. I wasn't sure you would be, the way you came through that door last night.
Thomas {warm, still}: If anyone asks, you were here with me, for your head. All night. It's true enough.
-> simon_back [if n4_thomas_simon]
-> simon_first

== simon_first [set n4_thomas_simon]
(He looks past you at the door, and lowers his voice.)
Thomas {grave}: Brother. I've seen Brother Simon out at night. Long after Compline, when he should be abed.
Thomas {warm, nod}: I don't say what it means. Only, keep an eye on him.
-> topics

== simon_back
Thomas {warm}: You've thought on what I told you? About Simon?
-> topics

== again
(Thomas looks up from the mortar. His fingers are stained green to the knuckle.)
Thomas {warm}: Back again? There's no supper to be late for tonight.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n4_thomas_simon_ask] What was Brother Simon doing out there? -> simon_ask
* [if died_crypt_pilgrim] [if not n4_thomas_crypt] I saw a bound man killed at the altar in the crypt. -> crypt
* [if not n4_thomas_edwin] How is Edwin? -> edwin

== simon_ask [set n4_thomas_simon_ask] [claim n4_thomas_keeps lie]
Thomas {grave}: On his knees on the flags by the chapter house, his lantern hooded. At an hour nobody prays.
Thomas {warm, still}: He's a quiet one, Simon. Quiet men keep things.
* [believe] I'll keep an eye on him, brother. -> simon_believed
* [press] Simon? He sings, and keeps his head down. What would he keep? -> simon_pressed

== simon_believed
Thomas {warm, nod}: Watch him, Alric. Don't go to him. Watch.
-> topics

== simon_pressed
Thomas {warm, still}: That's for you to find, not me. I only tell you what I see.
Thomas {warm}: Watch him, Alric. Don't go to him. Watch.
-> topics

== crypt [set n4_thomas_crypt] [trust thomas 5]
(He sets the pestle down very carefully, and hears you out.)
Thomas {sad}: A man bound, at the saint's own altar. God have mercy on him.
Thomas {grave, still}: Have you told the prior? Don't. Hugh would hang the porter for it and call it justice.
Thomas {warm}: Leave it with me. You did right to bring it here.
-> topics

== edwin [set n4_thomas_edwin]
Thomas {warm}: He came to me this morning for something to help him sleep, and poured it out of the window. I watched him do it.
Thomas {warm, nod}: He listens to you. Tell him to come to me after Matins, if he can't sleep.
-> topics

== leave
Thomas {warm}: Keep it between us, Alric. About Simon.
"
